xfce4-window-button-colors (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Adds the xfce4-window-button-colors-settings binary: a standalone
    GTK3 application, registered in the XFCE Settings Manager, that
    will host enabling/disabling the module and managing stored
    per-window colours without editing xfconf by hand. This release
    ships the application shell and packaging; the toggle and colour
    management UI land in a follow-up.
  * Adds libxfconf-0-dev to Build-Depends. The settings binary is the
    only target linking xfconf; src/core/ stays free of gtk_/xfconf_/
    wnck_ symbols, CI-enforced as before.

 -- Jorge Alonso <desarrollos@enfoquestic.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

xfce4-window-button-colors (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial package. Ships the GTK3 module and its CSS provider (slices
    1-3): colours are read from ~/.config/xfce4-window-button-colors/colors.css
    and painted onto matching launchers at panel start.
  * The context-menu item and the colour chooser are not implemented yet
    (slice 4), so colours must be written to colors.css by hand for now.
  * The module is installed but not enabled; see README for how to load it.

 -- Jorge Alonso <desarrollos@enfoquestic.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
